1
00:00:01,133 --> 00:00:02,300
<i>Now, maybe no one will suspect
that I'm still alive.</i>

2
00:00:02,433 --> 00:00:04,300
<i>Boss Matias, the coffin
really had a body inside.</i>

3
00:00:04,433 --> 00:00:05,367
<i> Send me evidence.</i>

4
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:08,033
<i>Sir, calm down!
We can talk about this!</i>

5
00:00:08,167 --> 00:00:09,433
<i> You're the boxer.</i>

6
00:00:09,567 --> 00:00:12,967
<i>Pretending to protect the woman,
but in truth, you're nothing!</i>

7
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:15,500
<i>We just want to ask
about your friend Jin Ho.</i>

8
00:00:15,633 --> 00:00:16,900
<i>- Where is he?
- I don't know.</i>

9
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:18,500
<i>We haven't contacted each other
for a long time.</i>

10
00:00:18,633 --> 00:00:21,667
<i>She seemed scared
when Yvette and Tomas entered.</i>

11
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:24,200
<i> [LIFE MONITOR BEEPING RAPIDLY]</i>

12
00:00:24,333 --> 00:00:26,533
<i> I need to silence Rebecca too.</i>

13
00:00:26,667 --> 00:00:29,200
<i>If you say anything
about what I did to you,</i>

14
00:00:29,333 --> 00:00:31,467
<i>I'll drag your two children
into this.</i>

15
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:33,333
<i> Do you understand me?</i>

16
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:34,567
<i> Good.</i>

17
00:00:36,667 --> 00:00:40,567
<i>["NEVER SAY DIE" BY KIM DE LEON
PLAYING]</i>

18
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:53,867
This is so frustrating.

19
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,633
I really thought
we'd get a lead on Jin Ho.

20
00:00:57,767 --> 00:00:58,733
Exactly!

21
00:00:58,867 --> 00:01:01,700
He's the only source I had
about him.

22
00:01:01,833 --> 00:01:04,533
Well, at least we tried, right?

23
00:01:04,667 --> 00:01:08,133
And in fairness,
it was a unique experience.

24
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:11,433
Imagine, we fought side by side
with Idol Eman.

25
00:01:11,567 --> 00:01:14,033
True. He's on another level.

26
00:01:14,167 --> 00:01:16,267
But in fairness, right?
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

27
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:20,333
He's quiet,
but he controls every move.

28
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:22,467
And he's humble.

29
00:01:22,600 --> 00:01:26,600
He's kind, not arrogant,
not trying to impress.

30
00:01:26,733 --> 00:01:29,667
And he helped right away
when someone was harassing us.

31
00:01:30,900 --> 00:01:34,733
And when he saw the guy
attacking us, he said...

32
00:01:34,867 --> 00:01:36,100
"Hey, that's a woman."

33
00:01:36,233 --> 00:01:38,367
You know?
Old-school but so cool!

34
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:41,500
Too bad we only got to be
with him briefly.

35
00:01:41,667 --> 00:01:44,100
Briefly, yet you have too much
to say.

36
00:01:44,233 --> 00:01:46,567
Of course, he's Idol Eman.

37
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:51,000
And it's true, he's principled.
That's what deserves admiration.

38
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:52,867
I'm principled too, you know.

39
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:55,067
Fine, we're all principled.

40
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:56,467
- Come on. I'm annoyed.
- Let's go.

41
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:58,233
We still don't have a lead
on Jin Ho.

42
00:02:02,100 --> 00:02:04,067
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:02:05,900 --> 00:02:07,067
Mom?

44
00:02:15,833 --> 00:02:17,567
Are you okay, Mom?

45
00:02:17,700 --> 00:02:19,500
Are you crying?

46
00:02:19,633 --> 00:02:21,133
I'll just call the doctor, okay?

47
00:02:21,267 --> 00:02:22,400
No need.

48
00:02:22,533 --> 00:02:25,200
I was giving her this.

49
00:02:25,333 --> 00:02:27,233
Maybe those are tears of joy.

50
00:02:30,533 --> 00:02:32,300
Chrysanthemums?

51
00:02:32,433 --> 00:02:33,833
Why this?

52
00:02:33,967 --> 00:02:35,067
What's the matter with you?

53
00:02:36,200 --> 00:02:37,500
Why, Yvette?

54
00:02:37,633 --> 00:02:40,433
It's associated with death.

55
00:02:41,867 --> 00:02:44,567
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

56
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:50,333
I'm sorry.

57
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:55,567
I didn't know
it was for the dead.

58
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,600
We still don't know
what happened to mommy.

59
00:03:00,467 --> 00:03:02,367
Yvette, I want her to feel safe.

60
00:03:03,433 --> 00:03:06,267
I want to get a security officer
watching over her here.

61
00:03:07,267 --> 00:03:09,567
I don't think it's necessary,
but...

62
00:03:10,767 --> 00:03:12,700
if that's what you want,
it's okay.

63
00:03:12,833 --> 00:03:14,700
- All right.
- That's a good idea.

64
00:03:15,733 --> 00:03:17,567
I'll send someone here.

65
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:19,233
No need, Thomas, I'll handle it.

66
00:03:19,367 --> 00:03:20,633
I know someone.

67
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:25,033
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

68
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:33,700
It's "rest in peace" for me.

69
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:36,800
Chief Lansang is quite good.

70
00:03:36,933 --> 00:03:39,733
He announced it
right at your funeral.

71
00:03:39,867 --> 00:03:42,200
We don't need to worry
about it anymore.

72
00:03:43,733 --> 00:03:46,667
Clarissa,
did you hear your daughter?

73
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,700
We don't need to worry
about this.

74
00:03:48,833 --> 00:03:50,700
Why do you still seem worried?

75
00:03:50,833 --> 00:03:52,567
Not really.

76
00:03:52,700 --> 00:03:58,200
But with all this talk
about death,

77
00:03:58,367 --> 00:04:00,600
I suddenly remembered
Ma'am Rebecca.

78
00:04:01,533 --> 00:04:03,767
- Because she almost died?
- [PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

79
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:06,433
If it did happen, maybe we'd be
mourning for her right now.

80
00:04:07,333 --> 00:04:09,800
- Hey.
- What really happened to her?

81
00:04:09,933 --> 00:04:11,867
Don't say that.

82
00:04:13,633 --> 00:04:16,800
But I really don't know.

83
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,867
But...

84
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,900
I can't imagine...

85
00:04:22,667 --> 00:04:24,600
That she'd do that to herself.

86
00:04:25,633 --> 00:04:29,767
Is someone trying to kill her,
or does she have enemies?

87
00:04:29,933 --> 00:04:34,300
From what I know
of Ma'am Rebecca, she's kind.

88
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:41,933
Yes, sometimes she's strict,
but that's normal at her age.

89
00:04:42,067 --> 00:04:45,467
Maybe I should visit her.

90
00:04:45,600 --> 00:04:49,733
If I see her,
maybe my worries will go away.

91
00:04:50,767 --> 00:04:52,500
Mom, I'll go with you.

92
00:04:57,633 --> 00:04:59,533
Why haven't I received
any updates

93
00:04:59,667 --> 00:05:01,300
on what I asked you to do?

94
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:03,700
I'm getting impatient!
Where are you?

95
00:05:03,833 --> 00:05:06,033
I just arrived at the hospital,
Berdugo.

96
00:05:06,167 --> 00:05:08,800
Do what I ordered you to do.

97
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:12,133
I don't want the risk
of that old woman recovering.

98
00:05:12,267 --> 00:05:15,533
So, make sure that
before the day ends,

99
00:05:15,667 --> 00:05:17,500
she's no longer alive!

100
00:05:17,633 --> 00:05:19,033
Understood, Berdugo.

101
00:05:19,167 --> 00:05:22,233
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

102
00:05:22,367 --> 00:05:24,433
You heard what Berdugo said?

103
00:05:24,567 --> 00:05:26,333
Do your job.

104
00:05:26,467 --> 00:05:27,600
Room 213.

105
00:05:27,733 --> 00:05:32,733
When the guard arrives,
find a way to get out of there.

106
00:05:32,867 --> 00:05:34,133
Go.

107
00:05:46,467 --> 00:05:49,433
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

108
00:05:52,967 --> 00:05:56,100
Miss, who are you looking for?

109
00:05:56,233 --> 00:05:59,000
I'm looking for Sir Eman.

110
00:05:59,133 --> 00:06:02,400
I wasn't able to thank him
yesterday for helping us,

111
00:06:02,533 --> 00:06:04,433
so I brought him food today.

112
00:06:04,567 --> 00:06:07,200
And because of that,
he even got reprimanded...

113
00:06:07,367 --> 00:06:08,633
Forget it.

114
00:06:10,333 --> 00:06:11,467
You're here.

115
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:12,700
Just call me Eman.

116
00:06:12,833 --> 00:06:15,067
I have training right now.
Want to join?

117
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:17,733
- Really? I can?
- Of course.

118
00:06:17,867 --> 00:06:19,533
- The two of us.
- Us?

119
00:06:19,667 --> 00:06:21,600
Yes, us.

120
00:06:21,733 --> 00:06:23,167
Let's train together.

121
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:26,267
Okay. Let's go...

122
00:06:26,400 --> 00:06:28,367
- Come on?
- Training...

123
00:06:31,867 --> 00:06:35,300
All right. I'll just talk to
the doctor when she comes out.

124
00:06:35,433 --> 00:06:36,300
Okay, Sir.

125
00:06:36,433 --> 00:06:40,800
Nurse, can you change
my mom's beddings?

126
00:06:40,967 --> 00:06:42,033
Okay, Sir.

127
00:06:42,167 --> 00:06:43,933
- Thanks.
- Okay.

128
00:06:50,367 --> 00:06:51,533
Andrew...

129
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:55,100
What are you doing here, Zoey?

130
00:06:55,233 --> 00:06:56,833
I just dropped by
before heading to work

131
00:06:56,967 --> 00:07:00,367
because I wanted
to apologize properly.

132
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:02,000
I admit it. I broke your trust.

133
00:07:02,133 --> 00:07:04,133
It was my fault leaving
Mommy Rebecca.

134
00:07:04,267 --> 00:07:05,433
Okay, stop.

135
00:07:06,333 --> 00:07:07,867
I should be the one apologizing.

136
00:07:09,167 --> 00:07:10,133
I overreacted.

137
00:07:10,267 --> 00:07:12,267
I shouldn't have gotten mad
at you.

138
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:15,300
I shouldn't even have given you
the responsibility

139
00:07:15,467 --> 00:07:16,767
to take care for my mom.

140
00:07:18,500 --> 00:07:21,167
Does that mean you're not mad
at me anymore?

141
00:07:22,867 --> 00:07:24,033
Yeah, we're okay.

142
00:07:24,767 --> 00:07:27,467
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

143
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:29,800
I'm happy we're okay again.

144
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,067
Me too.

145
00:07:33,267 --> 00:07:36,533
Go to work now.
You might be late.

146
00:07:36,667 --> 00:07:38,967
You know what? I'll buy coffee
across the street.

147
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:42,033
Want to come with me
so you can have coffee too?

148
00:07:45,567 --> 00:07:46,800
Jab.

149
00:07:46,933 --> 00:07:48,500
Jab, straight.

150
00:07:48,667 --> 00:07:50,400
Jab, straight.

151
00:07:50,533 --> 00:07:51,700
Jab, jab, straight.

152
00:07:53,067 --> 00:07:53,967
That's okay for now.

153
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:56,400
- [CHUCKLES]
- You've got moves too.

154
00:07:56,533 --> 00:07:57,667
Well, my dad's a cop,

155
00:07:57,800 --> 00:08:00,667
so he taught me basic boxing
and taekwondo.

156
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,833
You're really cool.

157
00:08:02,967 --> 00:08:06,467
I told my parents we met you.

158
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:09,267
My dad said he wants
to be your friend too.

159
00:08:09,400 --> 00:08:10,800
We're friends?

160
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,433
Sorry...

161
00:08:13,567 --> 00:08:18,633
I assumed we were friends
because you helped us,

162
00:08:18,767 --> 00:08:19,867
but maybe that's just me.

163
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,200
Who are you looking for?
Your boyfriend?

164
00:08:22,367 --> 00:08:24,200
He's not my boyfriend.

165
00:08:24,333 --> 00:08:26,733
I'm looking for Jin Ho.

166
00:08:26,867 --> 00:08:28,700
Sorry, I answered too quickly.

167
00:08:28,833 --> 00:08:31,233
No, I mean,
he's really just my friend.

168
00:08:31,367 --> 00:08:32,967
And I need to know something
about him,

169
00:08:33,100 --> 00:08:34,400
that's why I'm looking for him.

170
00:08:34,533 --> 00:08:36,267
You have so many friends.

171
00:08:36,400 --> 00:08:37,867
Not really.

172
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,833
I'm selective with friends.

173
00:08:39,967 --> 00:08:42,067
That's why I didn't expect
to be friends

174
00:08:42,200 --> 00:08:44,267
with Eman Bacosa Pacquiao.

175
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:45,700
It's just me.

176
00:08:45,833 --> 00:08:48,167
Really? Can I throw a punch?

177
00:08:48,300 --> 00:08:49,133
Jab, straight.

178
00:08:50,567 --> 00:08:52,133
Jab, straight.

179
00:08:52,267 --> 00:08:53,567
Punch here.

180
00:08:54,767 --> 00:08:57,100
- More. I'm fine.
- You okay?

181
00:08:57,233 --> 00:08:58,267
[THUDS]

182
00:09:00,467 --> 00:09:02,067
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

183
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:04,267
Doc.

184
00:09:05,367 --> 00:09:06,767
I'll just check the patient.

185
00:09:06,900 --> 00:09:08,567
Can you call a nurse?

186
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:11,500
I just want to know
if the medicine was given.

187
00:09:11,633 --> 00:09:14,133
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

188
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,267
Sorry.

189
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:25,900
Some of us have to go first.

190
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:29,367
[REBECCA WHIMPERING]

191
00:09:29,533 --> 00:09:31,033
[DOOR OPENS]

192
00:09:36,300 --> 00:09:38,333
What happened to my mom?

193
00:09:38,467 --> 00:09:40,233
I was just checking her line.

194
00:09:40,367 --> 00:09:43,767
Looks like she's hurting
from the way I held the IV.

195
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:46,767
- I'll go ahead. Sorry, Ma'am.
- Wait, wait.

196
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:48,500
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

197
00:09:48,633 --> 00:09:50,400
I don't think I know you.

198
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:52,900
Who are you, Doc?

199
00:09:53,467 --> 00:09:56,467
Sorry, I didn't introduce
myself. I'm Doc Reyes.

200
00:09:56,600 --> 00:09:58,833
I'm one of the hospital
residents.

201
00:09:58,967 --> 00:10:02,133
Anyway, I'll just check
at the nurse station.

202
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:03,400
I'll go ahead.

203
00:10:04,433 --> 00:10:06,600
[REBECCA WHIMPERING]

204
00:10:12,167 --> 00:10:13,167
Mom...

205
00:10:14,333 --> 00:10:15,333
Just relax.

206
00:10:15,633 --> 00:10:16,867
Thank you.

207
00:10:17,233 --> 00:10:19,733
Hey, maybe you need to go back
to training.

208
00:10:19,867 --> 00:10:21,567
I hope we still see each other.

209
00:10:23,267 --> 00:10:24,200
I hope so,

210
00:10:24,333 --> 00:10:26,633
and I hope we won't be
fighting anymore.

211
00:10:26,767 --> 00:10:27,633
Yes.

212
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:31,000
But it looks like
that's still far off.

213
00:10:31,133 --> 00:10:34,200
Anyway, just remember,
every time you fight,

214
00:10:34,367 --> 00:10:37,500
I'll watch and cheer for you.
I'll pray for you.

215
00:10:37,633 --> 00:10:39,633
- Promise?
- Promise.

216
00:10:42,233 --> 00:10:44,800
- Never say die?
- Never say die.

217
00:10:47,733 --> 00:10:51,033
I met Zoey, so I didn't notice
a doctor went inside.

218
00:10:51,167 --> 00:10:53,000
But the security said

219
00:10:53,133 --> 00:10:55,700
he saw the doctor pass by
the nurses' station.

220
00:10:55,833 --> 00:10:58,200
Maybe you're just
overthinking it.

221
00:10:58,333 --> 00:11:02,867
Didn't Doc Sandoval say they're
going to run some tests for mom?

222
00:11:03,167 --> 00:11:05,933
You know, I think you're tired.

223
00:11:06,533 --> 00:11:08,900
Go home first so you can rest.

224
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:10,467
I'm okay.

225
00:11:10,600 --> 00:11:12,967
But you're not getting
enough sleep.

226
00:11:13,400 --> 00:11:16,667
No, Yvette, I'm really fine.
You go home.

227
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:19,133
Stay with my niece and nephew.

228
00:11:19,267 --> 00:11:22,067
I'll update you
if there's progress here.

229
00:11:23,033 --> 00:11:25,967
But I suggest you have someone
stay with you.

230
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,300
Who do you want?

231
00:11:28,433 --> 00:11:35,867
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]

232
00:11:36,900 --> 00:11:39,000
Are you serious about
what you want?

233
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:43,400
You can't even walk properly,
yet you want to be a policeman?

234
00:11:43,567 --> 00:11:45,633
What are you saying?
I'll recover, okay?

235
00:11:45,767 --> 00:11:49,433
And besides,
Uncle Miguel said he'll help me.

236
00:11:49,567 --> 00:11:53,233
And when school starts,
I'll transfer to criminology.

237
00:11:53,367 --> 00:11:55,300
I'm already working
on the requirements.

238
00:11:55,433 --> 00:11:56,733
Well, come to think of it,

239
00:11:56,867 --> 00:11:59,233
you're smart and resourceful.

240
00:11:59,367 --> 00:12:00,933
You can do it.

241
00:12:01,800 --> 00:12:06,067
When Andrew finds out,
he'll be happy!

242
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:09,400
You know, we really support you
becoming a policeman.

243
00:12:10,500 --> 00:12:11,767
Thank you.

244
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:15,567
Are you with Andrew?

245
00:12:17,033 --> 00:12:18,600
Where did that question
come from?

246
00:12:18,733 --> 00:12:20,567
You know, you two are okay.

247
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:23,567
- [PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]
- You look good together.

248
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:27,467
By the way, that letter
I gave you from grandmother,

249
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:29,733
forget about it, okay?

250
00:12:29,867 --> 00:12:31,700
I only said that because...

251
00:12:31,833 --> 00:12:36,200
I felt like I was losing
a friend then...

252
00:12:37,667 --> 00:12:39,433
That's all.

253
00:12:39,567 --> 00:12:42,367
You know that won't happen.

254
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,467
We're friends for life.

255
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:49,033
You were my first friend
when I studied in Manila.

256
00:12:49,200 --> 00:12:51,433
Yes, you were so grumpy then!

257
00:12:51,567 --> 00:12:54,133
You know, that feistiness of
yours won't work with Andrew.

258
00:12:54,267 --> 00:12:56,233
You found your match.

259
00:12:58,633 --> 00:13:00,600
But you know,

260
00:13:00,733 --> 00:13:03,500
even if our friend is tough,

261
00:13:03,633 --> 00:13:08,433
I pity him because of
his mom's situation.

262
00:13:08,567 --> 00:13:10,000
It's okay.

263
00:13:10,133 --> 00:13:14,033
We're here to support him,
especially you.

264
00:13:16,100 --> 00:13:18,167
Believe it or not,

265
00:13:18,300 --> 00:13:22,167
I'm sure you're the one
he wants to be with.

266
00:13:22,333 --> 00:13:24,633
You're partners in crime, right?

267
00:13:25,967 --> 00:13:28,933
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

268
00:13:29,067 --> 00:13:32,100
Don't lose hope, Sir Andrew.

269
00:13:32,233 --> 00:13:34,067
- Just pray.
- [LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]

270
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:40,500
Good morning,
Ma'am Yvette, Sir Tomas.

271
00:13:40,633 --> 00:13:41,867
- Clarissa.
- [OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

272
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,367
Clarissa, why are you here?

273
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:47,000
Your husband's funeral
just ended, right?

274
00:13:47,133 --> 00:13:48,200
Yes, Ma'am.

275
00:13:48,333 --> 00:13:52,233
I've long accepted
that my husband is gone.

276
00:13:52,367 --> 00:13:53,967
So...

277
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:57,900
I really want to visit
Ma'am Rebecca.

278
00:13:58,067 --> 00:14:01,667
In fact, Joey also wants
to visit her too.

279
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,100
Where's Joey?

280
00:14:04,933 --> 00:14:10,000
Sir Andrew, she stayed up late
talking to Peter,

281
00:14:10,133 --> 00:14:11,967
so I didn't wake her.

282
00:14:13,933 --> 00:14:16,167
Has mom woken up?

283
00:14:16,300 --> 00:14:20,700
Early this morning,
but she went back to sleep.

284
00:14:20,833 --> 00:14:26,500
Well, I guess we can wake her up
so she can see us all.

285
00:14:26,833 --> 00:14:28,500
I'm sure she'll be happy.

286
00:14:29,467 --> 00:14:31,333
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

287
00:14:31,467 --> 00:14:32,600
Mom...

288
00:14:33,667 --> 00:14:34,933
Mommy...

289
00:14:35,067 --> 00:14:37,267
Mommy, we're here.

290
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:38,867
Wake up.

291
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:41,967
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

292
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,867
<i>If you say anything about
what I did to you,</i>

293
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,233
<i> I won't stop with you.</i>

294
00:14:58,367 --> 00:15:01,000
<i>I'll drag your two children
into this.</i>

295
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:05,300
Who are you?

296
00:15:06,567 --> 00:15:09,533
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

297
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:15,467
Who are you?

298
00:15:21,100 --> 00:15:22,633
Where am I?

299
00:15:22,767 --> 00:15:24,867
Mommy, you're in the hospital.

300
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:28,533
Don't you remember
what happened to you?

301
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:34,667
Mom, don't be afraid of me...

302
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:35,733
Mom...

303
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:37,600
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

304
00:15:37,733 --> 00:15:39,667
Mom, don't be afraid of us.

305
00:15:39,800 --> 00:15:41,233
Mom...

306
00:15:41,367 --> 00:15:42,600
Mom, we're your family.

307
00:15:42,733 --> 00:15:46,333
I'm Yvette, Mom,
your daughter, Mommy.

308
00:15:46,467 --> 00:15:48,467
We're not here to hurt you.

309
00:15:51,233 --> 00:15:53,900
Ma'am Rebecca, don't be afraid.

310
00:15:56,400 --> 00:16:00,133
They are your family.
They won't hurt you.

311
00:16:00,267 --> 00:16:01,300
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

312
00:16:01,433 --> 00:16:02,533
Mom...

313
00:16:02,667 --> 00:16:06,433
We love you so much.
We're not going to hurt you.

314
00:16:06,567 --> 00:16:07,967
Yes, Mom.

315
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:09,400
You're here...

316
00:16:09,567 --> 00:16:14,100
because we found you
in your room unconscious.

317
00:16:14,233 --> 00:16:16,500
What happened to you is still
a mystery for us.

318
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:20,467
Only you can tell us
what really happened.

319
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:22,500
- [UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]
- Can you try to remember?

320
00:16:23,867 --> 00:16:28,167
Doc, will my mom's memory
return?

321
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:30,300
When will she recover?

322
00:16:30,433 --> 00:16:34,133
I will refer you to a specialist
friend of mine.

323
00:16:34,267 --> 00:16:38,167
But as far as I know,
there's no definite time.

324
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:41,900
It can be days, months,
or even years.

325
00:16:42,067 --> 00:16:43,667
Or never?

326
00:16:43,800 --> 00:16:46,433
<i> Let's not lose hope.</i>

327
00:16:46,567 --> 00:16:51,167
Sir, maybe you can
show her things

328
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:54,167
that might trigger her memory

329
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:57,867
or tell her stories
from her past.

330
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,100
That can be really helpful.

331
00:17:00,233 --> 00:17:03,333
As long as she always has
someone with her,

332
00:17:03,467 --> 00:17:07,100
so if she asks questions,
someone can answer,

333
00:17:07,233 --> 00:17:09,567
making it easier for her.

334
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:10,867
I'll be here.

335
00:17:11,967 --> 00:17:13,600
I won't leave mom.

336
00:17:13,733 --> 00:17:15,533
Do you really not remember
anything?

337
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:34,800
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

338
00:17:42,600 --> 00:17:45,133
Darling, you seem in a hurry.
Where are you going?

339
00:17:46,733 --> 00:17:50,700
Mom told me that Ma'am Rebecca
is already talking,

340
00:17:50,867 --> 00:17:53,567
but she still doesn't remember
anything.

341
00:17:53,700 --> 00:17:55,067
She doesn't remember?

342
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:56,633
What? Amnesia?

343
00:17:56,767 --> 00:17:59,133
Seems like it.

344
00:17:59,267 --> 00:18:01,133
Poor woman.

345
00:18:01,267 --> 00:18:04,567
What really happened
to cause that?

346
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:08,567
That's what we still don't know.

347
00:18:08,700 --> 00:18:12,400
That's why Andrew is so worried
about her.

348
00:18:12,533 --> 00:18:14,200
You know, it happened to me too

349
00:18:14,333 --> 00:18:16,567
when we didn't know
where you were.

350
00:18:16,700 --> 00:18:19,033
I really thought you were gone.

351
00:18:19,167 --> 00:18:23,567
Good thing there were people
like Andrew who helped us.

352
00:18:23,733 --> 00:18:26,900
So now, you're the one
helping Andrew?

353
00:18:27,833 --> 00:18:28,967
Yes, Dad.

354
00:18:29,833 --> 00:18:31,133
Wait.

355
00:18:31,267 --> 00:18:34,067
I think it's not Rebecca
you want to see.

356
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:36,967
You want to see Andrew,
don't you?

357
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:38,800
- Is Andrew courting you?
- [PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

358
00:18:38,933 --> 00:18:39,967
Wow, Dad!

359
00:18:40,100 --> 00:18:42,467
I thought you'd sympathize
with me,

360
00:18:42,600 --> 00:18:44,767
- but you're just teasing me.
- [STAMMERS]

361
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:46,033
I'm just saying.

362
00:18:46,167 --> 00:18:49,867
I'm just asking if Andrew
is really courting you.

363
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,733
- What? Hey, dear!
- Yes?

364
00:18:51,867 --> 00:18:53,700
Tell me, okay?

365
00:18:54,733 --> 00:19:01,167
This photo, Mom, this was when
you won Journalist of the Year.

366
00:19:02,567 --> 00:19:10,300
I think it was your second or
third time winning that award.

367
00:19:11,767 --> 00:19:13,433
That's why you're my idol.

368
00:19:14,767 --> 00:19:16,967
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

369
00:19:17,100 --> 00:19:19,733
I really want to follow
in your footsteps.

370
00:19:20,967 --> 00:19:25,367
But of course,
sometimes we clash

371
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,233
because we want
different things.

372
00:19:35,033 --> 00:19:36,133
But...

373
00:19:37,233 --> 00:19:40,800
I always think about
what you told me, Mom.

374
00:19:41,833 --> 00:19:44,067
All your advice.

375
00:19:45,267 --> 00:19:47,167
And you know what?
Most of the time...

376
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:51,700
I realize you're right.

377
00:19:56,267 --> 00:19:57,433
Next.

378
00:20:00,467 --> 00:20:01,733
This one...

379
00:20:03,533 --> 00:20:05,567
These are your grandchildren,
Mom.

380
00:20:07,300 --> 00:20:10,900
They are the children of Yvette,
my sister.

381
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,667
You?

382
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:20,033
Do you have children?

383
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:24,967
Not yet, Mom.

384
00:20:25,100 --> 00:20:26,933
No wife yet.

385
00:20:27,067 --> 00:20:28,967
Not even a girlfriend.

386
00:20:31,733 --> 00:20:34,933
I want to marry someone who's...

387
00:20:36,100 --> 00:20:37,267
<i> Brave.</i>

388
00:20:38,867 --> 00:20:40,267
<i> Resourceful.</i>

389
00:20:44,067 --> 00:20:45,433
<i> Loving.</i>

390
00:20:46,533 --> 00:20:47,733
Like you.

391
00:20:51,600 --> 00:20:52,833
Me?

392
00:20:58,767 --> 00:21:00,200
Okay, next.

393
00:21:02,133 --> 00:21:04,633
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

394
00:21:06,367 --> 00:21:10,633
This one is Tomas...

395
00:21:13,733 --> 00:21:14,733
Mom?

396
00:21:14,867 --> 00:21:16,667
Is your head hurting?

397
00:21:19,367 --> 00:21:22,733
Okay, let's do this tomorrow.
Rest first, Mom.

398
00:21:25,700 --> 00:21:26,800
[GRUNTS]

399
00:21:29,533 --> 00:21:31,033
Wait.

400
00:21:31,167 --> 00:21:32,733
You should rest for now, Mom.

401
00:21:38,267 --> 00:21:41,333
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

402
00:21:45,033 --> 00:21:46,167
Mom...

403
00:21:47,133 --> 00:21:48,700
I know it's hard.

404
00:21:49,967 --> 00:21:53,133
But if you remember
what happened to you,

405
00:21:54,200 --> 00:21:55,633
please tell me.

406
00:21:57,333 --> 00:22:00,267
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

407
00:22:09,733 --> 00:22:10,633
- Andrew.
- Joey?

408
00:22:10,767 --> 00:22:11,633
Andrew.

409
00:22:11,767 --> 00:22:14,300
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

410
00:22:14,433 --> 00:22:17,567
How's your mom?
Has she remembered anything?

411
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,233
Not yet.

412
00:22:19,967 --> 00:22:22,500
But I'm trying to...

413
00:22:23,233 --> 00:22:24,267
make her remember.

414
00:22:25,433 --> 00:22:29,033
She gets tired, though,
so she fell asleep.

415
00:22:29,567 --> 00:22:30,900
And you, how are you?

416
00:22:31,033 --> 00:22:33,933
Here, imitating you.

417
00:22:34,067 --> 00:22:35,367
Imitating me?

418
00:22:35,500 --> 00:22:39,400
Because I remembered before,
when you had problems...

419
00:22:39,533 --> 00:22:41,233
even when you were tired,

420
00:22:41,367 --> 00:22:44,233
even when the situation
was so difficult...

421
00:22:44,367 --> 00:22:46,100
you never gave up.

422
00:22:46,233 --> 00:22:48,533
You always persevered.

423
00:22:48,700 --> 00:22:52,233
That's what I'm trying
to do now.

424
00:22:52,367 --> 00:22:54,800
The only reason
I managed back then

425
00:22:54,933 --> 00:22:59,133
was because people helped me
and supported me...

426
00:22:59,267 --> 00:23:01,300
and you were one of them.

427
00:23:01,433 --> 00:23:03,067
That's why now...

428
00:23:04,367 --> 00:23:06,433
you're the one going through
something,

429
00:23:06,567 --> 00:23:09,100
I'm here to support you.

430
00:23:09,233 --> 00:23:11,900
Even if sometimes
you get annoyed with me,

431
00:23:12,033 --> 00:23:14,000
it's okay, I won't leave you.

432
00:23:14,133 --> 00:23:15,267
Remember that.

433
00:23:16,900 --> 00:23:18,100
Thank you, Joey.

434
00:23:20,733 --> 00:23:24,700
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

435
00:23:38,467 --> 00:23:41,500
What do I have to do
to get rid of you, Joey?

436
00:23:42,700 --> 00:23:45,800
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

437
00:23:54,167 --> 00:23:55,467
Tomorrow, I'll try to bring
Peter

438
00:23:55,633 --> 00:23:57,900
so there's someone playful
around.

439
00:23:58,033 --> 00:23:59,500
Okay, thank you again.

440
00:24:02,667 --> 00:24:06,733
I forgot to return this to you.

441
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:09,100
You dropped it last time.

442
00:24:10,333 --> 00:24:13,700
[DREAMY MUSIC PLAYING]

443
00:24:13,833 --> 00:24:16,500
Wow, you still got that?

444
00:24:16,633 --> 00:24:18,433
I thought I lost it.

445
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:22,400
Did you know that was for you?

446
00:24:23,433 --> 00:24:24,933
One each for us.

447
00:24:25,200 --> 00:24:26,900
Lucky you picked it up.

448
00:24:27,033 --> 00:24:29,200
I don't think "luck"
is the right word.

449
00:24:29,367 --> 00:24:30,667
What then?

450
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:32,267
Fate.

451
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:36,267
It was destined to end up
with me.

452
00:24:37,300 --> 00:24:38,367
Really?

453
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:41,433
Wear it now.

454
00:24:41,567 --> 00:24:44,400
Okay. Wait, how do I?

455
00:24:44,533 --> 00:24:45,567
Here, let me.

456
00:24:45,700 --> 00:24:48,667
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

457
00:24:52,200 --> 00:24:53,467
There.

458
00:24:54,733 --> 00:24:56,000
Now we both have one.

459
00:25:03,667 --> 00:25:04,767
It's beautiful.

460
00:25:11,500 --> 00:25:14,467
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

461
00:25:18,267 --> 00:25:19,367
Are you okay?

462
00:25:19,500 --> 00:25:20,833
Don't pressure her.

463
00:25:20,967 --> 00:25:22,100
Don't interfere.

464
00:25:22,233 --> 00:25:24,700
If you're not going to help,
then don't meddle.

465
00:25:24,833 --> 00:25:26,367
How dare you talk to me
like that?

466
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:28,900
We can't just let Jin Ho go.

467
00:25:29,033 --> 00:25:31,533
He's dad's only lead
to the syndicate.

468
00:25:31,667 --> 00:25:34,367
Maybe he's just checking in
because he's spying on us.

469
00:25:34,500 --> 00:25:36,933
If so, he would've already told
the syndicate who you are.

470
00:25:37,100 --> 00:25:40,467
It was bothering me that this
woman's face looked familiar.

471
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:42,200
Let's go ahead
to the meeting place, okay?

472
00:25:42,333 --> 00:25:45,067
Then let's plan
how we'll corner Jin Ho.

473
00:25:45,200 --> 00:25:47,433
That's our target.
Let's follow him!

474
00:25:47,567 --> 00:25:49,633
- Andrew!
- Andrew! Let's split up!

475
00:25:49,767 --> 00:25:50,867
Andrew!

476
00:25:52,033 --> 00:25:52,800
Andrew!
